Z||000029||Mach10||09-08-2001||02:35 AM||||Geez, I leave for a few days, and find 28 topics to my name...<P>First, this post was sort of a misunderstanding. I left it alone anyway, as it's good to have stuff out in the open. It's not a flame thread. Simply what I do and do not like about the US. <P>Black88GT: It was late, I was tired, all I saw was more of what usually ticks me off. I've said what I felt needed to be said at the time. Not going to quibble about history. There was a war, lots of people died, the US made a decision to unleash a horrible new weapon on Japan. Maybe it was the right thing to do. Maybe it was the ONLY thing to do. I cannot find any way to justify it. As such, I take great offence when people toss that around. Civilians are still civilians, in my book. I'd have rathered that the US had vaporized Japans fleet, or a few of their military bases, rather than 2 major urban centers. But then, I wasn't there, and I am no military strategist. <BR>As for the Canadians at Overlord, I'm sorry if I mistook you, but it seemed pretty debasing to me at the time. If that wasn't your intent, then I cheerfully withdraw.<BR>Oh, and we aren't a smaller country. We're HUGE. But unfortunately, Polar bears don't EVER Register  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P><BR>MJ: Your knowledge of military history astounds me again. The sources that I was able to locate (mostly memorials, not too big on tactical details, just lists of names) indicated that the Juno defensive was more firmly entrenched than on Omaha. However, thinking back on this, it's possible that I mis-read and the meaning was better prepared than our canadian assault...<BR>Again, I bow to your far superior sources :}<BR>Oh, and thanks for the examples. <P>FieroNV: I'm not on a who's country is better rant. I was clarifying the impression (incorrect as it appeared) that I was fanatically anti-US. I will agree that the bombs ironically would have saved lives. I do question the judgement of dropping them on urban centers (see above). Again, I'm no tactitian. Maybe there WAS no better way. War is never pleasant, in any case.<P>Stimpy: The whole point of this post is now moot. It was a misunderstanding. Now it's an interesting Political debate. I see no flaming going on here. It's all clean, so far... Lighten up, have a beer :}<P>Formula: I agree. On all counts.<P>Thomas_l: "I suppose if the Japanese fleet had bigger gas tanks and <B>flew</B> north to attack Vancouver"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><BR>Am I the only one who caught that?!? :]<BR>I agree. Mutual ignorance is a big problem. I can go on a HUGE Cultural Anthro schpiel here explaining some of it, and the problems it causes but I'm far too tired[lazy] right now :}<BR>I agree with you, also.<P>Urchin: Took me the last boring half of my shift  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Jsocha: [I did have a small row of smilies, but I've reached my limit :{ ]<P>Pat's Dad:  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Frontal Lobe:  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Thanks. You saw the point  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>OcalaFiero: I was thinking along similar lines...<P>Artherd: I'm 1/8 Alien (long story...) Better watch what you say... ;}<P>Baldlobo: I figured I needed more red clothes. <P>Did I miss anyone?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000030||Fierowrecker||09-08-2001||07:20 AM||||I have loved all the PLACES I've been to, it's that some of the PEOPLE at those places were without brains...<BR>Although, I love every visit I have to Canada, much less of the brainless people there...<BR>And to think Canada has such a broader ethnic population than most countries I've been to...<BR>Must be an entrance exam to get into Canada?<BR>Course, Michigan IS a part of Canada, they just lost it in the war...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
