Z||000032||Tonker||09-08-2001||06:35 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B><BR>I bet you were a fan when we took care of the Japs for you, or the Nazi's for that matter.  While the Nazi's was more of a global endevour, I wonder how many Canadians stormed the beaches of Normandy?  I'm no historian but my guess is more Americans were there.<P>Just something to think about.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Congrats on picking the one thing that would really STEAM MY A$$! Where was the US in 1939-1941 When the Nazi were occupying most of Europe and had nearly cut off the supply lines to Britain. Let me tell you which North American country was in the trenches shedding blood then Black88GT. Canada. Don't go spouting drivel about Canda's war effort in WW II We were in it from the start. And don't give me that ****  about us not being there until they invaded France. Utter crap. <P>Don't get me wrong. The US won the war. They made an enormous war contribution even when they weren't actively involved hostilities throught the lend-lease program and sending supplies to Britain. Just don't slag Canada for not spilling our share of blood, man.<P>The US population in 1945 was 139,928,165. Canada's population was ~11,500,000. US casualties were 295,000 Canada 39,000. I'm not sure if it's a meaninful number but if you divide the casualties into the population Canada comes up higher Black88GT (US .21, CDA .34). Of course more Americans were there. The population of your country is 10 times larger than Canada's. Think, man! You were given a brain for a reason. Engage it. As for Japan, we were fighting them in Hong Kong in 1941.<P>Here's where my numbers are from: <A HREF="http://www.valourandhorror.com/DB/BACK/Casualties.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.valourandhorror.com/DB/BACK/Casualties.htm</A>   <A HREF="http://www.infoplease.com/year/1945.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.infoplease.com/year/1945.html</A>  <A HREF="http://british-forces.com/world_war2/otherfiles/commonwealth.html" TARGET=_blank>http://british-forces.com/world_war2/otherfiles/commonwealth.html</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Tonker (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||13
Z||000033||maryjane||09-08-2001||07:13 PM||||Tonker, I think this has already been resolved, see-dispute settled- in above reply. One little note tho. Of the 106 Victoria Crosses (Equivalent to our Medal Of Honor), awarded servicemen from Commonwealth Nations, ( I believe I read 17 nations in the Commonwealth at that time)13 were bestowed to members of Canada's armed forces- roughly half were awarded posthumusly. I don't think anyone really meant to belittle Canada's contribution or sacrifice in this endeavour. ||||reg||1
Z||000034||Tonker||09-08-2001||07:27 PM||||Sorry, I guess I took that a bit too personally. I guess I should make it a point to read the entire thread before posting...<BR>||||reg||1
